  "profile": "Astronomer specializing in exoplanet transit photometry and timing analysis, with emphasis on characterizing systematic effects from stellar activity. I develop Bayesian and machine learning pipelines to extract precise transit parameters from TESS, JWST, and ground-based data, specializing in transit timing variations (TTVs) and starspot-induced biases. As a lead contributor to international collaborations including the ExoClock Project and EXPLORE, I coordinate multi-site observing campaigns across 50+ countries. I teach computational methods and programming at the undergraduate level and maintain reproducible, open-source research workflows.",
